# Exact Hall-phase scan checkpoint

This checkpoint records the finite incidence audit implemented in
research/hall_phase_scan.py.

The scanner enumerates every monomer/dimer cell packing in a rectangular axial
triangular-lattice patch. It verifies, with integer arithmetic, both identities

\[
|S|-|N(S)|=\frac{m_3-b}{2}-\chi,
\qquad
\sum_v(4p_v+3q_v-12)=12\bigl(|S|-|N(S)|\bigr).
\]

The necessary local geometric cap of five cells incident at one lattice vertex was
enforced. It is only a necessary condition for realizing the blocker points by a
unit-separated configuration.

## Reproducible outputs

Command:

    python3 research/hall_phase_scan.py --width 2 --height 3

Output:

    patch=2x3 triangles=12 status=complete
    leaves=41068 valid_degree_leaves=41068 max_left_nullity=0 max_neighborhood_deficiency=0

Thus every cell packing in this complete \(2\times3\) state space has an incidence
matching saturating its selected cells. In particular, the degree-five cap does not
by itself create a Hall obstruction at this scale.

The deterministic prefix

    python3 research/hall_phase_scan.py --width 3 --height 3 --max-leaves 200000

returned

    patch=3x3 triangles=18 status=truncated
    leaves=200000 valid_degree_leaves=200000 max_left_nullity=0 max_neighborhood_deficiency=0

This second line is a bounded regression, not an exhaustive \(3\times3\) theorem.
The scan supports the existing conclusion that local degree and phase charge need a
larger-scale/global ingredient; it does not prove the Target A inequality
\(d_{\rm sc}\ge\Delta_\Lambda\).

## Degree-five regression outside the exhaustive window

The script also carries a fixed \(4\times4\) monomer pattern, selected by omitting
six elementary triangles. The exact witness command is

    python3 research/hall_phase_scan.py --show-degree-five-witness

and returns

    fixed_witness=4x4 triangles=32 cells=26 vertices=23 rank=23 left_nullity=3 max_vertex_incidence=5

This demonstrates that the local degree-five condition alone does not force a
matching of all cells. The witness is intentionally only an incidence pattern:
the 26 blocker points have not been placed and no diameter-optimality claim is
made. It is therefore a guardrail for the scaffold proof, not a counterexample
to Erdos #99.

There is an exact capacity reason this witness is not geometric. All 26 cells lie
in the \(4\times4\) lattice parallelogram \(K\), for which

\[
\operatorname{area}(K)+c_0\operatorname{per}(K)
=8\sqrt3+4\sqrt3=12\sqrt3,
\]

whereas 26 unit-separated points in \(K\) would require, by Oler,

\[
a_0(26-1)=\frac{25\sqrt3}{2}>12\sqrt3.
\]

Thus the first positive-nullity pattern is already excluded by finite packing
capacity. This is precisely why the global scaffold target must combine Hall
nullity with the surrounding hull/collar data rather than use local incidence
alone.
